    rule1Title: "1. Specify AISI 316L or 2205 Duplex Metallurgy for Continuous Peracetic Acid Zones",
    rule1Text: "Standard AISI 304 stainless steel lacks molybdenum and possesses a low Pitting Resistance Equivalent Number (PREN ~18). In warm (≥50°C) peracetic acid wash zones containing residual tap water chlorides (>50 ppm), the protective chromium oxide film undergoes micro-fissuring and catastrophic crevice pitting at weld seams. Always mandate AISI 316L (PREN ≥24.5) or 2205 Duplex for all chemical sanitizing modules.",
